" font-size="15" font-weight="400" fill="#374151" text-anchor="start">Depend on abstractions</text><rect x="50" y="420" width="480" height="380" rx="20" fill="#DBEAFE"/><circle cx="95" cy="470" r="30" fill="#1D4ED8"/><text x="95" y="481" class="s" font-size="32" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">S</text><rect x="140" y="440" width="370" height="60" rx="30.0" fill="#1D4ED8"/><text x="325.0" y="479.1" class="s" font-size="26" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">Single Responsibility</text><circle cx="75" cy="532" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="538" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">A class should have only one reason</text><text x="90" y="563" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">to change.</text><circle cx="75" cy="590" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="596" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">Each class does one job and does it</text><text x="90" y="621" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">well.</text><circle cx="75" cy="648" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="654" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">Easier to test, read and reuse.</text><rect x="75" y="738" width="430" height="40" rx="20" fill="#fff" stroke="#1D4ED8" stroke-width="2"/><text x="290" y="764" class="s" font-size="18" font-weight="800" fill="#1D4ED8" text-anchor="middle">Remember: One class, one job</text><rect x="550" y="420" width="1000" height="380" rx="20" fill="#F8FAFC" stroke="#CBD5E1" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="565" y="434" width="480" height="352" rx="14" fill="#FEF2F2" stroke="#DC2626" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="580" y="446" width="300" height="40" rx="20.0" fill="#B91C1C"/><text x="730.0" y="471.95" class="s" font-size="17" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">Before: breaks the principle</text><text x="582" y="518" class="m" 