 +<svg width="1600" height="2570" viewBox="0 0 1600 2570" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="SOLID principles in Java with before and after examples" xmlns:c2pa="http://c2pa.org/manifest"><style>.s{font-family:Inter,sans-serif}.m{font-family:"JetBrains Mono",monospace;font-weight:500}</style><rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="#ffffff"/><text x="50" y="70" class="s" font-size="40" font-weight="800"><tspan fill="#6B7280">Code</tspan><tspan fill="#EA580C">Trove</tspan></text><text x="50" y="150" class="s" font-size="64" font-weight="800" fill="#0F2A4A" text-anchor="start">SOLID Principles</text><rect x="50" y="168" width="520" height="8" rx="4" fill="#FACC15"/><rect x="1360" y="95" width="190" height="64" rx="32" fill="#FFEDD5" stroke="#EA580C" stroke-width="2"/><text x="1455" y="137" class="s" font-size="30" font-weight="800" fill="#9A3412" text-anchor="middle">in Java</text><rect x="50" y="210" width="270" height="70" rx="35.0" fill="#6D28D9"/><text x="185.0" y="254.8" class="s" font-size="28" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">What is SOLID?</text><rect x="340" y="200" width="1210" height="90" rx="18" fill="#EDE9FE"/><text x="365" y="242" class="s" font-size="22" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">Five object-oriented design principles, popularized by Robert C. Martin (Uncle Bob),</text><text x="365" y="274" class="s" font-size="22" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">that make code easier to understand, extend, test and maintain.</text><rect x="50" y="310" width="292" height="76" rx="14" fill="#DBEAFE" stroke="#1D4ED8" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="88" cy="348" r="24" fill="#1D4ED8"/><text x="88" y="358" class="s" font-size="28" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">S</text><text x="124" y="340" class="s" font-size="15" font-weight="800" fill="#1D4ED8" text-anchor="start">Single Responsibility</text><text x="124" y="364" class="s" font-size="15" font-weight="400" fill="#374151" text-anchor="start">One class, one job</text><rect x="354" y="310" width="292" height="76" rx="14" fill="#DCFCE7" stroke="#15803D" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="392" cy="348" r="24" fill="#15803D"/><text x="392" y="358" class="s" font-size="28" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">O</text><text x="428" y="340" class="s" font-size="15" font-weight="800" fill="#15803D" text-anchor="start">Open / Closed</text><text x="428" y="364" class="s" font-size="15" font-weight="400" fill="#374151" text-anchor="start">Extend, don't edit</text><rect x="658" y="310" width="292" height="76" rx="14" fill="#FEF3C7" stroke="#B45309" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="696" cy="348" r="24" fill="#B45309"/><text x="696" y="358" class="s" font-size="28" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">L</text><text x="732" y="340" class="s" font-size="15" font-weight="800" fill="#B45309" text-anchor="start">Liskov Substitution</text><text x="732" y="364" class="s" font-size="15" font-weight="400" fill="#374151" text-anchor="start">Subtypes keep promises</text><rect x="962" y="310" width="292" height="76" rx="14" fill="#FCE7F3" stroke="#BE185D" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="1000" cy="348" r="24" fill="#BE185D"/><text x="1000" y="358" class="s" font-size="28" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">I</text><text x="1036" y="340" class="s" font-size="15" font-weight="800" fill="#BE185D" text-anchor="start">Interface Segregation</text><text x="1036" y="364" class="s" font-size="15" font-weight="400" fill="#374151" text-anchor="start">Small interfaces</text><rect x="1266" y="310" width="292" height="76" rx="14" fill="#EDE9FE" stroke="#6D28D9" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="1304" cy="348" r="24" fill="#6D28D9"/><text x="1304" y="358" class="s" font-size="28" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">D</text><text x="1340" y="340" class="s" font-size="15" font-weight="800" fill="#6D28D9" text-anchor="start">Dependency Inversion</text><text x="1340" y="364" class="s" font-size="15" font-weight="400" fill="#374151" text-anchor="start">Depend on abstractions</text><rect x="50" y="420" width="480" height="380" rx="20" fill="#DBEAFE"/><circle cx="95" cy="470" r="30" fill="#1D4ED8"/><text x="95" y="481" class="s" font-size="32" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">S</text><rect x="140" y="440" width="370" height="60" rx="30.0" fill="#1D4ED8"/><text x="325.0" y="479.1" class="s" font-size="26" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">Single Responsibility</text><circle cx="75" cy="532" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="538" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">A class should have only one reason</text><text x="90" y="563" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">to change.</text><circle cx="75" cy="590" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="596" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">Each class does one job and does it</text><text x="90" y="621" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">well.</text><circle cx="75" cy="648" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="654" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">Easier to test, read and reuse.</text><rect x="75" y="738" width="430" height="40" rx="20" fill="#fff" stroke="#1D4ED8" stroke-width="2"/><text x="290" y="764" class="s" font-size="18" font-weight="800" fill="#1D4ED8" text-anchor="middle">Remember: One class, one job</text><rect x="550" y="420" width="1000" height="380" rx="20" fill="#F8FAFC" stroke="#CBD5E1" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="565" y="434" width="480" height="352" rx="14" fill="#FEF2F2" stroke="#DC2626" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="580" y="446" width="300" height="40" rx="20.0" fill="#B91C1C"/><text x="730.0" y="471.95" class="s" font-size="17" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">Before: breaks the principle</text><text x="582" y="518" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">class</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Report</tspan> {</text><text x="582" y="545" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">  <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">String</tspan> build() { }</text><text x="582" y="572" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">  <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">void</tspan> saveToFile() { }</text><text x="582" y="599" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">  <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">void</tspan> sendEmail() { }</text><text x="582" y="626" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">}</text><text x="582" y="653" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#15803D">// 3 reasons to change</tspan></text><rect x="1060" y="434" width="475" height="352" rx="14" fill="#F0FDF4" stroke="#16A34A" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="1075" y="446" width="300" height="40" rx="20.0" fill="#15803D"/><text x="1225.0" y="471.95" class="s" font-size="17" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">After: follows the principle</text><text x="1077" y="518" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">class</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">ReportBuilder</tspan> { <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">String</tspan> build() { } }</text><text x="1077" y="545" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">class</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">ReportSaver</tspan> { <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">void</tspan> save() { } }</text><text x="1077" y="572" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">class</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">ReportMailer</tspan> { <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">void</tspan> send() { } }</text><text x="1077" y="599" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"></text><text x="1077" y="626" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#15803D">// one reason to change each</tspan></text><rect x="50" y="824" width="480" height="380" rx="20" fill="#DCFCE7"/><circle cx="95" cy="874" r="30" fill="#15803D"/><text x="95" y="885" class="s" font-size="32" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">O</text><rect x="140" y="844" width="370" height="60" rx="30.0" fill="#15803D"/><text x="325.0" y="883.1" class="s" font-size="26" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">Open / Closed</text><circle cx="75" cy="936" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="942" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">Open for extension, closed for</text><text x="90" y="967" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">modification.</text><circle cx="75" cy="994" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="1000" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">Add behavior with new classes</text><text x="90" y="1025" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">instead of editing tested code.</text><circle cx="75" cy="1052" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="1058" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">Use interfaces and polymorphism.</text><rect x="75" y="1142" width="430" height="40" rx="20" fill="#fff" stroke="#15803D" stroke-width="2"/><text x="290" y="1168" class="s" font-size="18" font-weight="800" fill="#15803D" text-anchor="middle">Remember: Extend, don't edit</text><rect x="550" y="824" width="1000" height="380" rx="20" fill="#F8FAFC" stroke="#CBD5E1" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="565" y="838" width="480" height="352" rx="14" fill="#FEF2F2" stroke="#DC2626" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="580" y="850" width="300" height="40" rx="20.0" fill="#B91C1C"/><text x="730.0" y="875.95" class="s" font-size="17" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">Before: breaks the principle</text><text x="582" y="922" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">double</tspan> area(<tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Shape</tspan> s) {</text><text x="582" y="949" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">  <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">if</tspan> (s <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">instanceof</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Circle</tspan> c)</text><text x="582" y="976" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">    <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">return</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Math</tspan>.<tspan fill="#1D4ED8">PI</tspan> * c.r * c.r;</text><text x="582" y="1003" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">  <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">else</tspan> <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">if</tspan> (s <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">instanceof</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Square</tspan> q)</text><text x="582" y="1030" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">    <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">return</tspan> q.side * q.side;</text><text x="582" y="1057" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">  <tspan fill="#15803D">// new shape = edit this method</tspan></text><text x="582" y="1084" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">}</text><rect x="1060" y="838" width="475" height="352" rx="14" fill="#F0FDF4" stroke="#16A34A" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="1075" y="850" width="300" height="40" rx="20.0" fill="#15803D"/><text x="1225.0" y="875.95" class="s" font-size="17" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">After: follows the principle</text><text x="1077" y="922" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">interface</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Shape</tspan> { <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">double</tspan> area(); }</text><text x="1077" y="949" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">class</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Circle</tspan> <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">implements</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Shape</tspan> {</text><text x="1077" y="976" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">  <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">public</tspan> <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">double</tspan> area() {</text><text x="1077" y="1003" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">    <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">return</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Math</tspan>.<tspan fill="#1D4ED8">PI</tspan> * r * r;</text><text x="1077" y="1030" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">  }</text><text x="1077" y="1057" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">}</text><text x="1077" y="1084" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#15803D">// add Triangle, touch nothing old</tspan></text><rect x="50" y="1228" width="480" height="380" rx="20" fill="#FEF3C7"/><circle cx="95" cy="1278" r="30" fill="#B45309"/><text x="95" y="1289" class="s" font-size="32" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">L</text><rect x="140" y="1248" width="370" height="60" rx="30.0" fill="#B45309"/><text x="325.0" y="1287.1" class="s" font-size="26" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">Liskov Substitution</text><circle cx="75" cy="1340" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="1346" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">Subtypes must be usable wherever the</text><text x="90" y="1371" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">parent type is expected.</text><circle cx="75" cy="1398" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="1404" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">A subclass keeps the parent's</text><text x="90" y="1429" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">contract.</text><circle cx="75" cy="1456" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="1462" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">No surprises: don't throw or weaken</text><text x="90" y="1487" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">behavior.</text><rect x="75" y="1546" width="430" height="40" rx="20" fill="#fff" stroke="#B45309" stroke-width="2"/><text x="290" y="1572" class="s" font-size="18" font-weight="800" fill="#B45309" text-anchor="middle">Remember: Subtypes keep promises</text><rect x="550" y="1228" width="1000" height="380" rx="20" fill="#F8FAFC" stroke="#CBD5E1" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="565" y="1242" width="480" height="352" rx="14" fill="#FEF2F2" stroke="#DC2626" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="580" y="1254" width="300" height="40" rx="20.0" fill="#B91C1C"/><text x="730.0" y="1279.95" class="s" font-size="17" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">Before: breaks the principle</text><text x="582" y="1326" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">class</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Bird</tspan> { <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">void</tspan> fly() { } }</text><text x="582" y="1353" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">class</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Penguin</tspan> <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">extends</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Bird</tspan> {</text><text x="582" y="1380" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">  <tspan fill="#B45309">@Override</tspan> <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">void</tspan> fly() {</text><text x="582" y="1407" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">    <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">throw</tspan> <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">new</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">UnsupportedOperationException</tspan>();</text><text x="582" y="1434" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">  }</text><text x="582" y="1461" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827">}</text><text x="582" y="1488" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#15803D">// Penguin breaks Bird's contract</tspan></text><rect x="1060" y="1242" width="475" height="352" rx="14" fill="#F0FDF4" stroke="#16A34A" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="1075" y="1254" width="300" height="40" rx="20.0" fill="#15803D"/><text x="1225.0" y="1279.95" class="s" font-size="17" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">After: follows the principle</text><text x="1077" y="1326" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">interface</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Bird</tspan> { <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">void</tspan> eat(); }</text><text x="1077" y="1353" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">interface</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Flyer</tspan> { <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">void</tspan> fly(); }</text><text x="1077" y="1380" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">class</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Sparrow</tspan> <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">implements</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Bird</tspan>, <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Flyer</tspan> { }</text><text x="1077" y="1407" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">class</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Penguin</tspan> <tspan fill="#7C3AED" font-weight="700">implements</tspan> <tspan fill="#1D4ED8">Bird</tspan> { }</text><text x="1077" y="1434" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"></text><text x="1077" y="1461" class="m" xml:space="preserve" font-size="16" fill="#111827"><tspan fill="#15803D">// every subtype works as its parent</tspan></text><rect x="50" y="1632" width="480" height="380" rx="20" fill="#FCE7F3"/><circle cx="95" cy="1682" r="30" fill="#BE185D"/><text x="95" y="1693" class="s" font-size="32" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">I</text><rect x="140" y="1652" width="370" height="60" rx="30.0" fill="#BE185D"/><text x="325.0" y="1691.1" class="s" font-size="26" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">Interface Segregation</text><circle cx="75" cy="1744" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="1750" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">Prefer small, focused interfaces.</text><circle cx="75" cy="1777" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="1783" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">No class is forced to implement</text><text x="90" y="1808" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">methods it does not use.</text><circle cx="75" cy="1835" r="4" fill="#111827"/><text x="90" y="1841" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">Many specific interfaces beat one</text><text x="90" y="1866" class="s" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#1F2937" text-anchor="start">big one.</text><rect x="75" y="1950" width="430" height="40" rx="20" fill="#fff" stroke="#BE185D" stroke-width="2"/><text x="290" y="1976" class="s" font-size="18" font-weight="800" fill="#BE185D" text-anchor="middle">Remember: Small interfaces</text><rect x="550" y="1632" width="1000" height="380" rx="20" fill="#F8FAFC" stroke="#CBD5E1" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="565" y="1646" width="480" height="352" rx="14" fill="#FEF2F2" stroke="#DC2626" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="580" y="1658" width="300" height="40" rx="20.0" fill="#B91C1C"/><text x="730.0" y="1683.95" class="s" font-size="17" font-weight="800" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">Before: breaks the principle</text><text x="582" y="1730" class="m" xml:space="preserve"